    // ===================== THE THREE FROZEN GATE READERS =====================
    // The manual's result for VMFL078 is Figure .78.2, "Comparison of X-Velocity
    // along the vertical centerline in the symmetry plane" (p.224, PDF p.238).
    //
    // VMFL078 read that line at the MID-SPAN plane only, and graded GATE FAIL.
    // R2 reads the SAME 201 frozen abscissae on THREE vertical lines at x = 0.5:
    //
    //    midspanProbe    z = 0.50   -- the cube's mid-span; what the figure's own
    //                                  caption names.  LIMB B, the primary gate.
    //    quarterProbe    z = 0.25   -- the cube's quarter-span; equivalently the
    //                                  MID-PLANE OF THE MANUAL'S HALF DOMAIN
    //                                  (breadth 0.5).  LIMB C, the hypothesis test.
    //    quarter75Probe  z = 0.75   -- the MIRROR of z = 0.25 about the mid-span.
    //                                  Read ONLY so that limb D can measure whether
    //                                  the full cube's own solution is symmetric.
    //                                  It is not an extra chance at agreement: the
    //                                  pre-registration gates C on z = 0.25 alone.
    //
    // THE ABSCISSAE ARE THE 201 FROZEN VALUES OF VMFL078, LIFTED VERBATIM from the
    // committed controlDict.template so that limb B is LIKE-FOR-LIKE with the frozen
    // VMFL078_LIMB_B_PREREGISTRATION.md (freeze 98ba5a532e30ecee4e6da3a61be8a7dcf2e4a8dc).
    // Not one abscissa is re-chosen, and the band is not re-derived (rule 2).
    //
    // interpolationScheme cellPoint is LOAD-BEARING and is carried from VMFL078:
    // VMFL054 MEASURED that the default containing-cell sampler reads a slightly
    // different physical location on each mesh of an r = 2 family and polluted the
    // observed order (p ~ 0.21, GCI ~ 11 %).  Deleting this line voids the triple.
    //
    // The window excludes y = 0 and y = 1: those carry EXACTLY the imposed boundary
    // values at every level, and VERIFICATION_CHARTER sec.2a forbids gating on a
    // quantity derivable by construction from its own inputs.

